/**
 * expect: no finding of its own. The scope root, and the composition that makes JD-N01 real: the
 * mixing of moments only exists once these three are assembled.
 *
 * Two findings. JD-N01: this composition rests on leaves that exist at different moments, and
 * performance's e_timings gives no way to tell which. JD-N02: provenance and performance disagree
 * about the metrics, one treating them as committed and one as written by a run, which also BLOCKS
 * the JD-M01 those two leaves would otherwise be, since aligning them would silently pick a winner.
 *
 * The negative, and the reason this case exists: performance's e_metrics names a file that appears
 * nowhere in this repository, and it must draw **nothing at all**. It is well named, it says when it
 * exists, and a case discharged from CI would find it exactly where it says. Any finding about a
 * missing file means the skill has started searching the tree, which it must never do.
 */
load "quality.jd"
load "provenance.jd"
load "performance.jd"

justification release is assemble(quality, provenance, performance) {
    conclusionLabel: "The release meets its quality and performance targets"
    strategyLabel:   "Specification, provenance and performance together cover the release"
}
